      <revisionDesc>
          <change when="2016-10-06T05:55:42-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready.</change>
          <change when="2016-10-06T05:06:52-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/pheilpor">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - Checked on digital image shared by Claytor. Reading Εὐημ̣έ̣ρ̣[ο]υ̣ is much more likely that Εὐηνείου, which is probably a ghost name. Use of iota adscript elsewhere in this papyrus pleads for the reading τῶι τοῦ. Approved (and approved in a previous iteration by James Cowey).</change>
          <change when="2016-10-06T05:00:08-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Submit - corrected l. 15 from τῷ ἐμοῦ to the expected τῶι τοῦ, a normal use of the article before someone previously named.  In l. 16, I suggest Εὐημ̣έ̣ρ̣[ο]υ̣ instead of the otherwise unattested Εὐηνείου. Translation entered as well.</change>
          <change when="2014-12-19T23:22:39.484-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">corrected l. 15 from τῷ ἐμοῦ to τῶι τε; cf. the τε in l. 13.  The switch from objective to subjective style in the body of a grapheion contract would be anomalous (though not unprecedented).  Entered translation, though line numbers were not showing up properly in preview.</change>
